course: dictionary
lesson: 12896
title: Equilibrium: balance and calm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Equilibrium is a state of balance. Things are in equilibrium when opposite forces or amounts are equal, so nothing changes. «The scales are in equilibrium» means both sides weigh the same, so the scales stay level.
explain: A book lying still on a table is in equilibrium. The pull of gravity down is cancelled out by the table pushing up. A boat moving at a steady speed on calm water is also in equilibrium, because the forces on it balance.
explain: Equilibrium can also describe a calm, steady mind. «After the wobble, the tightrope walker slowly found her equilibrium again» means she became calm and steady once more. When you meet a hard word, look for the balance or the calm in the sentence.
fact: Equilibrium means a state of balance, where opposite forces or amounts are equal.
fact: «The scales are in equilibrium» means both sides are equal, so nothing changes.
fact: In maths, an equation is like scales in equilibrium: what you do to one side, you do to the other.
fact: In chemistry, equilibrium is when changes in two directions happen at the same rate, so the mixture stays the same overall.
fact: Equilibrium can also mean a calm, steady state of mind, as in «she lost her equilibrium».
exercise: «The scales are in equilibrium.» What does equilibrium mean here? | Everything is very noisy | One side is much heavier than the other | *Both sides are balanced and equal | The scales are broken
exercise: A book sits still on a table. Why is it in equilibrium? | Someone is holding it up | It is very heavy | It is moving very fast | *The pushes and pulls on it cancel out
exercise: In maths, what must you do to keep an equation in equilibrium? | *Do the same to the other side | Change only one side | Ignore the other side | Take away the equals sign
test: «She lost her equilibrium and nearly fell off the wobbly wall.» What does lost her equilibrium mean here? | She fell asleep on the wall | *She could no longer keep her balance | She found a new ball to play with | She ran very fast along the wall
test: When the water flowing into a pond and out of it happens at the same rate, the water level stays the same. What is the pond in? | Friction | Gravity | Confusion | *Equilibrium
exam: «After the wobble, the tightrope walker slowly found her equilibrium again.» What does equilibrium mean here? | Being very loud | Walking backwards | Falling off the rope | *Being calm and steady, able to balance again
